{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Two-block polarisation forms of the tree-level overlaps F_Psi (ABJM su(4) alternating chain)\n\n**Status (2026-10-12).** The shared Wolfram kernel died during this session (extension-host out of memory; Wolfram Engine licence expired, not renewed), so **only the cells of sections 0-1 were run in Wolfram** (the results below them are real kernel output). Every other code cell is written in full but **has not been run**; under each of them the result is pasted as markdown from the python/numpy re-computation of the same algorithm (scripts in `checks/twoblock-polforms/`). Rerun the notebook top to bottom after renewing the licence; the markdown results are what the cells should reproduce. All Wolfram symbols are prefixed `pf`.\n\n**What this notebook establishes** (details in section 13): for every saved highest-weight cyclic state at L = 2, 3, 4 pairs and every M = 0..L, the two-block overlap F_Psi(v2,u2;v3,u3;M) is, exactly (to 1e-14), a polynomial in the eight Borel-covariant building blocks a2, a3, d2, d3 (first/last components), mv, mu (2x2 leading/trailing minors), p23, p32 (cross pairings), plus p22, p33 if the pairs are not BPS. The exponents are fixed by weight and degree; the number of independent structures per (state, M) is a short explicit formula; the coefficients are the reduced structure constants tabulated below. Data files: `data/abjm-twoblock-forms.json` (python, complete) and `data/abjm-twoblock-forms.wxf` (written by section 11, unrun).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 0. Set-up, conventions, data\n\nChain `A F A F ...` with `L` pairs (site 1 = A), pair `k` = sites `(2k-1, 2k)`. Bras are row vectors, the overlap is the bilinear contraction `bra . psi` (no conjugation). Group action on bras: A site `v -> v g`, F site `u -> u g^{-T}`; the pairing `v.u` is invariant. The saved states (`data/abjm-hw-states.wxf`) are highest-weight: annihilated by the global `E_ij`, `i<j`, with `rho_A(E_ij) = e_ij`, `rho_F(E_ij) = -e_ji`; an A site `e_i` carries weight `+eps_i`, an F site `e_j` carries `-eps_j`.\n\nThe object studied here is the two-block overlap\n\n`F_Psi(v2,u2;v3,u3;M) = <(v2 x u2)^(L-M) (x) (v3 x u3)^M | Psi>`\n\n(first `L-M` pairs carry `(v2,u2)`, last `M` pairs carry `(v3,u3)`), a polynomial of multidegree `(L-M, L-M, M, M)` in the four 4-vectors. Vector components are `pfv2[i]`, `pfu2[i]`, `pfv3[i]`, `pfu3[i]`.\n\n**Where things ran.** Exploration and the data file `data/abjm-twoblock-forms.json` come from python (numpy, sympy; the Wolfram kernel is shared). The notebook redoes the computation in Wolfram (symbolic for L = 2, 3; pointwise for L = 4) and cross-checks against the JSON. All coefficients are **numerical** (the saved states are accurate to ~1e-13); structural statements (exponents, vanishing patterns) are exact in the sense of a gap of more than 10 orders of magnitude between zero and non-zero coefficients.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pfDir = \"C:/Users/pryan/git-projects/abjm-c123/Paul/Mathematica/su4-alternating\";\npfData = Import[FileNameJoin[{pfDir, \"data\", \"abjm-hw-states.wxf\"}], \"WXF\"];\npfStates = <|2 -> pfData[\"L2\"], 3 -> pfData[\"L3\"], 4 -> pfData[\"L4\"]|>;\npfJSON = Import[FileNameJoin[{pfDir, \"data\", \"abjm-twoblock-forms.json\"}], \"RawJSON\"];\n{pfV2, pfU2, pfV3, pfU3} = {Table[pfv2[i], {i, 4}], Table[pfu2[i], {i, 4}], Table[pfv3[i], {i, 4}], Table[pfu3[i], {i, 4}]};\npfVars = Join[pfV2, pfU2, pfV3, pfU3];\npfVV = {pfV2, pfV3}; pfUU = {pfU2, pfU3};\nGrid[{{\"pairs L\", \"number of saved HW cyclic states\", \"psi length\"},\n   Sequence @@ Table[{L, Length[pfStates[L]], Length[pfStates[L][[1]][\"psi\"]]}, {L, 2, 4}],\n   {\"data description\", Length[StringSplit[pfData[\"description\"]]] , \"words (read in the data file)\"},\n   {\"python JSON keys\", Length[Keys[pfJSON]], StringRiffle[Keys[pfJSON], \", \"]}},\n Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (real Wolfram output, ran):**\n\n| pairs L | # saved HW cyclic states | psi length |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 6 | 256 |\n| 3 | 26 | 4096 |\n| 4 | 152 | 65536 |\n| data description | 121 | words (read in the data file) |\n| python JSON keys | 6 | description, generated, conventions, L2, L3, L4 |",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. Check the conventions on the saved states\n\nSparse index lists (`pfPrepAll`: per state the digit matrix of the non-zero components and their values), the global generators `E_ij = sum_sites rho(E_ij)` applied directly on the digit representation, and the weight of every non-zero component. Expected: `E_ij psi = 0` for `i<j` (HW), every component has weight `w`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pfWeightRows[digs_, L_] := Total[Table[If[OddQ[s], 1, -1] IdentityMatrix[4][[digs[[All, s]]]], {s, 2 L}]];\npfPrep[psi_, L_] := Module[{rules = Most[ArrayRules[SparseArray[psi]]]}, {IntegerDigits[rules[[All, 1, 1]] - 1, 4, 2 L] + 1, rules[[All, 2]]}];\npfPrepAll = Association[Table[L -> (pfPrep[#[\"psi\"], L] & /@ pfStates[L]), {L, 2, 4}]];\n(* global E_ij psi on the sparse digit representation: A site (odd): e_ij, F site (even): -e_ji *)\npfApplyE[{digs_, vals_}, L_, i_, j_] := Module[{pw = 4^Range[2 L - 1, 0, -1], keys = {}, wts = {}, sel, d2},\n  Do[sel = Flatten[Position[digs[[All, s]], If[OddQ[s], j, i]]];\n   If[sel =!= {}, d2 = digs[[sel]]; d2[[All, s]] = If[OddQ[s], i, j];\n    AppendTo[keys, d2 . pw]; AppendTo[wts, If[OddQ[s], 1, -1] vals[[sel]]]], {s, 2 L}];\n  If[keys === {}, 0., Max[Abs[Values[GroupBy[Thread[Flatten[keys] -> Flatten[wts]], First -> Last, Total]]]]]];\npfHWcheck[L_] := Module[{defect, wok},\n  defect = Max[Table[pfApplyE[pfPrepAll[L][[k]], L, i, j], {k, Length[pfStates[L]]}, {i, 3}, {j, i + 1, 4}]];\n  wok = And @@ Table[Union[pfWeightRows[pfPrepAll[L][[k, 1]], L]] === {pfStates[L][[k]][\"w\"]}, {k, Length[pfStates[L]]}];\n  {L, Length[pfStates[L]], ScientificForm[defect, 3], wok}];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[pfHWcheck[L], {L, 2, 4}], {\"L\", \"# states\", \"max |E_ij psi|, i<j (all six)\", \"all components have weight w\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (real Wolfram output, ran before the kernel died):**\n\n| L | # states | max abs(E_ij psi), i<j (all six) | all components have weight w |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 6 | 5.52e-15 | True |\n| 3 | 26 | 1.25e-15 | True |\n| 4 | 152 | 4.56e-15 | True |\n\nThe conventions of the task (HW, weights, rho_A = e_ij, rho_F = -e_ji) hold for all 184 states.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. F as a polynomial in the 16 components (L = 2, 3: symbolic)\n\n`pfOverlapP` contracts the sparse state with a list of `2L` site vectors (`pfSiteVecs` puts block 2 on the first `L-M` pairs, block 3 on the last `M`). With symbolic vectors it returns the polynomial `F_Psi` in `pfv2[i], pfu2[i], pfv3[i], pfu3[i]` (no BPS condition imposed; coefficients below 1e-12 chopped). The BPS condition `v2.u2 = v3.u3 = 0` is imposed at the end (section 5).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pfSiteVecs[L_, M_, {v2_, u2_, v3_, u3_}] := Flatten[Table[If[k <= L - M, {v2, u2}, {v3, u3}], {k, L}], 1];\npfOverlapP[{digs_, vals_}, L_, vecs_List] := vals . (Times @@ Table[vecs[[s]][[digs[[All, s]]]], {s, 2 L}]);\npfFsym[L_, k_, M_] := Chop[Expand[pfOverlapP[pfPrepAll[L][[k]], L, pfSiteVecs[L, M, {pfV2, pfU2, pfV3, pfU3}]]], 10^-12];\npfFpolys = Association[Flatten[Table[{L, k, M} -> pfFsym[L, k, M], {L, 2, 3}, {k, Length[pfStates[L]]}, {M, 0, L}]]];\npfCoefRules[F_] := CoefficientRules[F, pfVars];\npfNterms[L_] := Table[Length[pfCoefRules[pfFpolys[{L, k, M}]]], {k, Length[pfStates[L]]}, {M, 0, L}];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{L, Length[Select[Keys[pfFpolys], First[#] == L &]], Max[pfNterms[L]], Count[Flatten[pfNterms[L]], 0]}, {L, 2, 3}], {\"L\", \"# polynomials (state, M)\", \"max # terms in F (no BPS)\", \"# identically zero\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (python re-computation, threshold 1e-12; Wolfram cell not run):**\n\n| L | # polynomials (state, M) | max # terms in F (no BPS) | # identically zero |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 18 | 28 | 4 |\n| 3 | 104 | 88 | 28 |",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Borel invariance and torus covariance on the polynomials\n\nThe HW trick says `F(v n, u n^{-T}) = F(v,u)` for every upper-unitriangular `n` acting simultaneously on all four vectors. Infinitesimally (`n = 1 + eps e_ij`, `i<j`): `v_j -> v_j + eps v_i`, `u_i -> u_i - eps u_j`, i.e. the derivation `D_ij = sum_{v in {v2,v3}} v_i d/dv_j - sum_{u in {u2,u3}} u_j d/du_i` must annihilate `F`. Torus: every monomial of `F` must have weight `w` (v_i counts `+eps_i`, u_i counts `-eps_i`). Checked as polynomials for all six `D_ij` and every state and `M`, `L = 2, 3`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pfDer[F_, i_, j_] := Expand[Sum[pfVV[[b, i]] D[F, pfVV[[b, j]]] - pfUU[[b, j]] D[F, pfUU[[b, i]]], {b, 2}]];\npfMaxCoef[expr_] := With[{cr = CoefficientRules[expr, pfVars]}, If[cr === {}, 0., Max[Abs[cr[[All, 2]]]]]];\npfWeightOfExp[e_] := Table[e[[i]] - e[[4 + i]] + e[[8 + i]] - e[[12 + i]], {i, 4}];\npfBorelCheck[L_] := Module[{keys = Select[Keys[pfFpolys], First[#] == L &], maxD, wbad},\n  maxD = Max[Table[Max[Table[pfMaxCoef[pfDer[pfFpolys[key], i, j]], {i, 3}, {j, i + 1, 4}]], {key, keys}]];\n  wbad = Count[keys, key_ /; With[{ws = Union[pfWeightOfExp /@ pfCoefRules[pfFpolys[key]][[All, 1]]]}, ws =!= {} && ws =!= {pfStates[L][[key[[2]]]][\"w\"]}]];\n  {L, Length[keys], ScientificForm[maxD, 3], wbad}];\nGrid[Prepend[pfBorelCheck /@ {2, 3}, {\"L\", \"# (state, M) polynomials\", \"max |coeff of D_ij F|, all 6 pairs i<j\", \"# torus-weight mismatches\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (python: same derivations on dict-polynomials; also sympy symbolic for the three simple roots; Wolfram cell not run):**\n\n| L | # (state, M) polynomials | max abs coeff of D_ij F, all 6 pairs | # torus-weight mismatches |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 18 | 1.2e-14 | 0 |\n| 3 | 104 | 4.2e-15 | 0 |\n| 4 (python only) | 760 | 3.3e-14 | 0 |\n\nsympy (16 symbols, simple roots only): 6.4e-15 (L=2), 3.3e-15 (L=3). F is exactly Borel invariant and torus covariant with weight w.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. Borel-invariant building blocks and the fit of F\n\nCandidates (all N+-invariant, torus-covariant):\n\n| block | weight | meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `a2 = (v2)_1`, `a3 = (v3)_1` | `eps_1` | first components of the A vectors |\n| `d2 = (u2)_4`, `d3 = (u3)_4` | `-eps_4` | last components of the F vectors |\n| `mv = (v2)_1 (v3)_2 - (v2)_2 (v3)_1` | `eps_1+eps_2` | leading 2x2 minor of the A vectors |\n| `mu = (u2)_3 (u3)_4 - (u2)_4 (u3)_3` | `-eps_3-eps_4` | trailing 2x2 minor of the F vectors |\n| `p22, p23, p32, p33` | 0 | pairings `v_a . u_b` (`p22 = p33 = 0` for BPS pairs) |\n\nWeights and degrees fix the exponents completely: with `n2 = L-M`, `n3 = M`, `e5 = w_2` (power of `mv`), `e6 = -w_3` (power of `mu`), the monomial `a2^e1 a3^e2 d2^e3 d3^e4 mv^e5 mu^e6 p22^e7 p23^e8 p32^e9 p33^e10` has `e1 = n2-e5-e7-e8`, `e2 = n3-e5-e9-e10`, `e3 = n2-e6-e7-e9`, `e4 = n3-e6-e8-e10` (all `>= 0`), and `e1+e2+e5 = w_1`, `-(e3+e4+e6) = w_4`. `pfMonos` enumerates them. `F` is fitted by linear least squares at 60 random unit-norm points (BPS points: `u -> u - (v.u)/(v.conj v) conj v`); the fit is repeated with and without the BPS condition. The residual measures how well `F` lies in the span; a vanishing `F` where no monomial exists tests completeness (an independent completeness check by dimension counting is in section 12).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pfInvNames = {\"a2\", \"a3\", \"d2\", \"d3\", \"mv\", \"mu\", \"p22\", \"p23\", \"p32\", \"p33\"};\npfInvVals[{v2_, u2_, v3_, u3_}] := {v2[[1]], v3[[1]], u2[[4]], u3[[4]], v2[[1]] v3[[2]] - v2[[2]] v3[[1]], u2[[3]] u3[[4]] - u2[[4]] u3[[3]], v2 . u2, v2 . u3, v3 . u2, v3 . u3};\npfInvSym = pfInvVals[{pfV2, pfU2, pfV3, pfU3}];\npfMonoVal[vals_, mon_] := Times @@ (Power @@@ Select[Transpose[{vals, mon}], #[[2]] > 0 &]);\npfMonos[L_, M_, w_, bps_] := Module[{n2 = L - M, n3 = M, e5 = w[[2]], e6 = -w[[3]], res = {}},\n  If[e5 >= 0 && e6 >= 0,\n   Do[With[{e1 = n2 - e5 - e7 - e8, e2 = n3 - e5 - e9 - e10, e3 = n2 - e6 - e7 - e9, e4 = n3 - e6 - e8 - e10},\n      If[Min[e1, e2, e3, e4] >= 0 && e1 + e2 + e5 == w[[1]] && -(e3 + e4 + e6) == w[[4]], AppendTo[res, {e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6, e7, e8, e9, e10}]]],\n    {e7, 0, If[bps, 0, L]}, {e8, 0, L}, {e9, 0, L}, {e10, 0, If[bps, 0, L]}]];\n  res];\nSeedRandom[20261012];\npfRandUnit[] := Normalize[RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 4]];\npfRandPoint[bps_] := Module[{v2, u2, v3, u3}, {v2, u2, v3, u3} = Table[pfRandUnit[], 4];\n  If[bps, u2 = u2 - (v2 . u2)/(v2 . Conjugate[v2]) Conjugate[v2]; u3 = u3 - (v3 . u3)/(v3 . Conjugate[v3]) Conjugate[v3]];\n  {v2, u2, v3, u3}];\npfPtsBPS = Table[pfRandPoint[True], 60]; pfPtsGen = Table[pfRandPoint[False], 60];\npfAinv[L_, M_, w_, bps_] := pfAinv[L, M, w, bps] = Module[{mons = pfMonos[L, M, w, bps], pts = If[bps, pfPtsBPS, pfPtsGen], A},\n  If[mons === {}, <|\"mons\" -> {}, \"rank\" -> 0|>,\n   A = Table[pfMonoVal[pfInvVals[pt], mon], {pt, pts}, {mon, mons}];\n   <|\"mons\" -> mons, \"A\" -> A, \"pinv\" -> PseudoInverse[A], \"rank\" -> MatrixRank[A]|>]];\npfFvals[L_, k_, M_, pts_] := Map[pfOverlapP[pfPrepAll[L][[k]], L, pfSiteVecs[L, M, #]] &, pts];\npfFit[L_, k_, M_, bps_] := Module[{w = pfStates[L][[k]][\"w\"], d, F, c},\n  d = pfAinv[L, M, w, bps]; F = pfFvals[L, k, M, If[bps, pfPtsBPS, pfPtsGen]];\n  If[d[\"mons\"] === {}, <|\"mons\" -> {}, \"c\" -> {}, \"res\" -> 0., \"Fmax\" -> Max[Abs[F]], \"rank\" -> 0|>,\n   c = d[\"pinv\"] . F; <|\"mons\" -> d[\"mons\"], \"c\" -> c, \"res\" -> Max[Abs[d[\"A\"] . c - F]], \"Fmax\" -> Max[Abs[F]], \"rank\" -> d[\"rank\"]|>]];\nGrid[{{\"example: allowed BPS monomials, L=3, M=1, w=(2,0,0,-2)\", pfMonos[3, 1, {2, 0, 0, -2}, True]},\n  {\"same, no BPS condition: number of monomials\", Length[pfMonos[3, 1, {2, 0, 0, -2}, False]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (python; Wolfram cell not run):** allowed BPS monomials for L=3, M=1, w=(2,0,0,-2): `{{2,0,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,0}, {1,1,2,0,0,0,0,1,0,0}}`, i.e. `a2^2 d2 d3 p32` and `a2 a3 d2^2 p23`; without the BPS condition: 4 monomials (adding `p22`/`p33` terms). BPS test points satisfy `v.u = 0` to < 1e-12 (asserted).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 4b. Fit every state, every M, with and without the BPS condition (L = 2, 3, 4)\n\n`pfFits[{L, k, M, bps}]` holds the allowed monomials (exponent lists in the order `a2 a3 d2 d3 mv mu p22 p23 p32 p33`), the fitted coefficients, the fit residual and `max |F|`. For `L = 4` the polynomial is never expanded: `F` is evaluated pointwise from the sparse state (`pfOverlapP` with numerical vectors). Checks: (i) the residual of the fit is at the level of rounding, (ii) where **no** invariant monomial of the right weight and degree exists, `F` vanishes identically, (iii) the monomial values are linearly independent (full rank).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pfFits = Association[Flatten[Table[{L, k, M, bps} -> pfFit[L, k, M, bps], {L, 2, 4}, {k, Length[pfStates[L]]}, {M, 0, L}, {bps, {True, False}}]]];\npfFitSummary[L_] := Module[{ent = Select[Normal[pfFits], #[[1, 1]] == L &], withm, without},\n  withm = Select[ent, #[[2]][\"mons\"] =!= {} &]; without = Select[ent, #[[2]][\"mons\"] === {} &];\n  {L, Length[ent], Length[withm], ScientificForm[Max[#[[2]][\"res\"] & /@ withm], 3], Length[without], ScientificForm[Max[#[[2]][\"Fmax\"] & /@ without], 3], Count[withm, e_ /; e[[2]][\"rank\"] < Length[e[[2]][\"mons\"]]]}];\nGrid[Prepend[pfFitSummary /@ {2, 3, 4}, {\"L\", \"# fits (state, M, BPS/full)\", \"# with allowed monomials\", \"max fit residual (unit-norm vectors)\", \"# with no allowed monomial\", \"max |F| there (must vanish)\", \"# rank-deficient monomial sets\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (python, same fit; Wolfram cell not run):**\n\n| L | # fits (state, M, BPS/full) | # with allowed monomials | max fit residual | # with no allowed monomial | max abs(F) there (must vanish) | # rank-deficient |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 36 | 24 | 3.4e-15 | 12 | 2.4e-16 | 0 |\n| 3 | 208 | 114 | 2.3e-16 | 94 | 1.3e-16 | 0 |\n| 4 | 1520 | 770 | 3.9e-16 | 750 | 4.0e-16 | 0 |\n\nSo `F` lies exactly in the span of the monomials of the ten (BPS: eight) invariants for all 184 states and all M, and vanishes identically wherever no such monomial exists.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Exact polynomial identity (L = 2, 3) and the BPS normal form\n\nFor `L = 2, 3` the fit is promoted to an identity between polynomials in the 16 components: `F - sum_k c_k I_k` (all ten invariants, no BPS condition) must have all coefficients at rounding level. With the BPS condition `F` is only defined modulo the ideal `(v2.u2, v3.u3)`; the remainder of `F - sum_BPS c_k I_k` under `PolynomialReduce` (lexicographic, leading terms `v2_1 u2_1`, `v3_1 u3_1`) must vanish.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pfPolyG[f_] := Total[MapThread[#1 Times @@ (pfInvSym^#2) &, {f[\"c\"], f[\"mons\"]}]];\npfIdentityFull[L_, k_, M_] := pfMaxCoef[Expand[pfFpolys[{L, k, M}] - pfPolyG[pfFits[{L, k, M, False}]]]];\npfIdealGens = {pfV2 . pfU2, pfV3 . pfU3};\npfIdentityBPS[L_, k_, M_] := Module[{r},\n  r = Last[PolynomialReduce[Expand[pfFpolys[{L, k, M}] - pfPolyG[pfFits[{L, k, M, True}]]], pfIdealGens, pfVars, MonomialOrder -> Lexicographic]];\n  pfMaxCoef[Expand[r]]];\npfIdRes = Table[{L, ScientificForm[Max[Table[pfIdentityFull[L, k, M], {k, Length[pfStates[L]]}, {M, 0, L}]], 3], ScientificForm[Max[Table[pfIdentityBPS[L, k, M], {k, Length[pfStates[L]]}, {M, 0, L}]], 3]}, {L, 2, 3}];\nGrid[Prepend[pfIdRes, {\"L\", \"max |coeff| of F - sum c_k I_k (16-variable polynomial, ten invariants)\", \"max |coeff| of remainder of F - sum_BPS c_k I_k mod (v2.u2, v3.u3)\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (python on dict-polynomials, normal form by eliminating `v_1 u_1`; also checked symbolically with sympy for L = 2, 3; Wolfram cell not run):**\n\n| L | max abs coeff of F - sum c_k I_k (16 variables) | max abs coeff of BPS remainder |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 9.6e-15 | 4.2e-15 |\n| 3 | 2.2e-15 | 3.9e-15 |\n| 4 (python only) | 1.2e-14 | 3.9e-14 |\n\nsympy (16 symbols, `F - sum c I` expanded, coefficients of the JSON rounded to 15 digits): 8.7e-15 (L=2), 4.9e-15 (L=3). So F, with and without the BPS condition, is a *polynomial* in the Borel-covariant building blocks, as an identity in the 16 components.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. F for every state and M (invariant form) and the reduced form F/F_vac\n\nNotation in the tables: `a2 a3 d2 d3 mv mu p22 p23 p32 p33` are the invariants of section 4 (products written as `a2 d3 p32`), coefficients are numerical with the saved phase of the state (largest component real positive). `F_vac = (a2 d2)^(L-M) (a3 d3)^M` is the overlap of the vacuum state, so `F/F_vac` is a polynomial in the four scale- and Borel-invariant ratios\n\n`x = p23/(a2 d3)`, `y = p32/(a3 d2)`, `μv = mv/(a2 a3)`, `μu = mu/(d2 d3)`,\n\nand its coefficients are the *reduced structure constants* (polarisation independent): each monomial `a2^e1 ... p32^e9` of F is `F_vac x^e8 y^e9 μv^e5 μu^e6`. Only rows with `F != 0` are listed (`|c| > 1e-9`; the gap between zero and non-zero coefficients is more than 10 orders of magnitude). By cyclicity `F(M)` and `F(L-M)` carry the same information (section 9), both are tabulated for L = 2, 3; for L = 4 the rows `M = 3, 4` are the mirror images of `M = 1, 0` and are left to the data file.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "pfThr = 10^-9;\npfNZ[f_] := Select[Transpose[{f[\"mons\"], f[\"c\"]}], Abs[#[[2]]] > pfThr &];\npfNum[x_] := If[Abs[x - Round[x]] < 10^-9, ToString[Round[x]], ToString[NumberForm[x, 6]]];\npfC[c_] := Module[{r = Chop[Re[c], 10^-11], i = Chop[Im[c], 10^-11]},\n  Which[i == 0, pfNum[r], r == 0, pfNum[i] <> \" I\", True, \"(\" <> pfNum[r] <> If[i < 0, \" - \", \" + \"] <> pfNum[Abs[i]] <> \" I)\"]];\npfMonStr[mon_] := StringRiffle[Flatten[MapThread[Which[#2 == 0, {}, #2 == 1, {#1}, True, {#1 <> \"^\" <> ToString[#2]}] &, {pfInvNames, mon}]], \" \"];\npfFormStr[f_] := With[{nz = pfNZ[f]}, If[nz === {}, \"0\", StringRiffle[(pfC[#[[2]]] <> If[pfMonStr[#[[1]]] === \"\", \"\", \" \" <> pfMonStr[#[[1]]]]) & /@ nz, \"  +  \"]]];\npfPow[name_, e_] := Which[e == 0, {}, e == 1, {name}, True, {name <> \"^\" <> ToString[e]}];\npfRedMon[m_] := StringRiffle[Join[pfPow[\"x\", m[[8]]], pfPow[\"y\", m[[9]]], pfPow[\"μv\", m[[5]]], pfPow[\"μu\", m[[6]]]], \" \"];\npfRedStr[f_] := With[{nz = pfNZ[f]}, If[nz === {}, \"0\", StringRiffle[(pfC[#[[2]]] <> If[pfRedMon[#[[1]]] === \"\", \"\", \" \" <> pfRedMon[#[[1]]]]) & /@ nz, \"  +  \"]]];\npfDynStr[L_, k_] := StringRiffle[ToString /@ pfStates[L][[k]][\"dyn\"], \",\"];\npfEstr[L_, k_] := ToString[NumberForm[pfStates[L][[k]][\"E\"], {7, 4}]];\npfTable[L_, Ms_] := Grid[Prepend[Join @@ Reap[Do[With[{f = pfFits[{L, k, M, True}]}, If[pfNZ[f] =!= {}, Sow[{k, pfDynStr[L, k], pfEstr[L, k], M, pfFormStr[f], pfRedStr[f]}]]], {k, Length[pfStates[L]]}, {M, Ms}]][[2]],\n   {\"#\", \"Dynkin [p,q,r]\", \"E_MZ\", \"M\", \"F (BPS pairs) in the invariants\", \"F/F_vac in x, y, μv, μu\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left];\n(* L = 2: BPS form and the form without the BPS condition side by side *)\nGrid[Prepend[Join @@ Reap[Do[With[{f = pfFits[{2, k, M, True}], g = pfFits[{2, k, M, False}]}, If[pfNZ[g] =!= {}, Sow[{k, pfDynStr[2, k], pfEstr[2, k], M, pfFormStr[f], pfFormStr[g]}]]], {k, 6}, {M, 0, 2}]][[2]],\n  {\"#\", \"Dynkin [p,q,r]\", \"E_MZ\", \"M\", \"F, BPS pairs (p22 = p33 = 0)\", \"F, no BPS condition\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result L = 2 (python; Wolfram cell not run).** The `[1,0,1]` pair (states 3, 4) and the two singlets (5, 6) are seen only at `M = 1` for BPS pairs; without the BPS condition also `M = 0, 2` through `p22`, `p33`:\n\n| # | Dynkin | E_MZ | M | F, BPS pairs (p22 = p33 = 0) | F, no BPS condition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 2,0,2 | 0.0000 | 0 | 1 a2^2 d2^2 | 1 a2^2 d2^2 |\n| 1 | 2,0,2 | 0.0000 | 1 | 1 a2 a3 d2 d3 | 1 a2 a3 d2 d3 |\n| 1 | 2,0,2 | 0.0000 | 2 | 1 a3^2 d3^2 | 1 a3^2 d3^2 |\n| 2 | 0,2,0 | 16.0000 | 1 | -0.5 mv mu | -0.5 mv mu |\n| 3 | 1,0,1 | 12.0000 | 0 | 0 | (0.288675 - 0.5 I) a2 d2 p22 |\n| 3 | 1,0,1 | 12.0000 | 1 | 0.288675 a3 d2 p23 + 0.288675 a2 d3 p32 | 0.288675 a3 d2 p23 + (-0.144338 - 0.25 I) a3 d3 p22 + (-0.144338 - 0.25 I) a2 d2 p33 + 0.288675 a2 d3 p32 |\n| 3 | 1,0,1 | 12.0000 | 2 | 0 | (0.288675 - 0.5 I) a3 d3 p33 |\n| 4 | 1,0,1 | 12.0000 | 0 | 0 | (0.288675 + 0.5 I) a2 d2 p22 |\n| 4 | 1,0,1 | 12.0000 | 1 | 0.288675 a3 d2 p23 + 0.288675 a2 d3 p32 | 0.288675 a3 d2 p23 + (-0.144338 + 0.25 I) a3 d3 p22 + (-0.144338 + 0.25 I) a2 d2 p33 + 0.288675 a2 d3 p32 |\n| 4 | 1,0,1 | 12.0000 | 2 | 0 | (0.288675 + 0.5 I) a3 d3 p33 |\n| 5 | 0,0,0 | 20.0000 | 0 | 0 | 0.316228 p22^2 |\n| 5 | 0,0,0 | 20.0000 | 1 | 0.158114 p23 p32 | 0.158114 p23 p32 + 0.158114 p22 p33 |\n| 5 | 0,0,0 | 20.0000 | 2 | 0 | 0.316228 p33^2 |\n| 6 | 0,0,0 | 4.0000 | 1 | -0.204124 p23 p32 | -0.204124 p23 p32 + 0.204124 p22 p33 |\n\nClosed forms (|c|^2 recognised as rationals): `[2,0,2]` vacuum 1; `[0,2,0]` `-1/2 mv mu`; `[1,0,1]` `(a3 d2 p23 + a2 d3 p32)/sqrt(12)`; singlets `p23 p32/sqrt(40)` (E=20) and `-p23 p32/sqrt(24)` (E=4).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
